    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51732" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθεῖς</span></b> , for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθ᾽
		εἷς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one by one,
				one after antoher</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>3 Ma.</u>
				5.34
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἷς καθεῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Marc.</u>
					14.19
				</span></i>
			, etc.: formed backwards from the neut. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἓν καθέν</span>, noted by <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Sol.</u>
				9
			</span></i>.</div>
